Let’s talk about SonarQube.

𝐒𝐨, 𝐰𝐡𝐚𝐭 𝐞𝐱𝐚𝐜𝐭𝐥𝐲 𝐢𝐬 𝐒𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐫𝐐𝐮𝐛𝐞?

SonarQube is a code quality and security analysis platform.
When you run a SonarQube scan, it looks for:

1.	Bugs (logic errors, bad patterns)
2.	Security vulnerabilities
3.	Code smells (maintainability issues)
4.	Duplicated code
5.	Code coverage (via test reports)

It doesn’t run your application.
It reads your code and applies thousands of rules.

𝐖𝐡𝐲 𝐝𝐨 𝐭𝐞𝐚𝐦𝐬 𝐮𝐬𝐞 𝐒𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐫𝐐𝐮𝐛𝐞?

Because code reviews don’t scale.
Humans miss things.
SonarQube doesn’t.

𝐈𝐭 𝐠𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐬 𝐭𝐞𝐚𝐦𝐬:

•	A single definition of code quality
•	Objective, repeatable checks
•	Early feedback (before production)
•	Most importantly — it introduces Quality Gates.

𝐖𝐡𝐚𝐭 𝐢𝐬 𝐚 𝐐𝐮𝐚𝐥𝐢𝐭𝐲 𝐆𝐚𝐭𝐞?
A Quality Gate is a set of rules like:
•	No new critical bugs
•	No new security vulnerabilities
•	Minimum test coverage
If the gate fails, the build should not pass.

𝐐𝐮𝐚𝐥𝐢𝐭𝐲 𝐆𝐚𝐭𝐞𝐬 𝐝𝐞𝐜𝐢𝐝𝐞:
•	Pass → pipeline moves forward
•	Fail → fix the code first
